        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): keep read warning args previews UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `read` tool validation warning preview must be both UTF-16 safe and visibly truncated when raw string args exceed the 200-code-unit warning budget. The earlier safe-slice follow-up still measured truncation with `for...of`, which counts Unicode code points. For `\"😀\".repeat(101)`, the safe slice shortened 202 UTF-16 code units to 200, but the code-point count stayed below the limit and omitted the ellipsis.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe warning now detects truncation with JavaScript string `.length`, matching the UTF-16 code-unit contract used by `truncateUtf16Safe`. The existing safe slice and console sanitization remain unchanged. A regression test exercises the production `handleToolExecutionStart` path with 101 astral characters and verifies 100 complete emoji plus `…`, with no lone surrogate.\n\n## User Impact\n\nRead-tool validation warnings remain well-formed at emoji/astral boundaries and consistently show when oversized arguments were truncated.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact tested head: `da74bd8b81a4f0722e929e2b45c77820f40a9590`\n- Before fix: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts` failed only the new astral-only regression; received 100 emoji without `…`.\n- After fix: the same command passed all 123 tests in the file (`123 passed`, 20.1s wall time).\n- The regression calls production `handleToolExecutionStart` with `args: \"😀\".repeat(101)` and expects exactly `\"😀\".repeat(100) + \"…\"`; it also rejects lone high or low surrogates.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- `.\\\\node_modules\\\\.bin\\\\oxfmt.cmd --check src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`: pass.\n- `.\\\\node_modules\\\\.bin\\\\oxlint.cmd src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.ts src/agents/embedded-agent-subscribe.handlers.tools.test.ts`: pass.\n\nKnown proof gap: the mandatory isolated autoreview helper was attempted twice but did not return before 120s and 300s timeouts. No autoreview finding was produced; focused behavior, formatting, lint, and diff checks above completed successfully.\n",
        "branch": "codex/read-tool-args-preview-utf16",
